Now I admit I've occasionally got it wrong myself, but still; when someone
has a good idea, the first step is to _test it_. Not to tell people about
it, and especially not to edit a wiki to put untested information in it.

(I am not suggesting you personally put this bogosity in the wiki.)

The primary factor that controls what order objects enter a bag is the
"packorder" option (tested with all four menustyles, although I doubt
anyone uses "traditional" anymore). The most important approach, if you
are worried about doing this, is to put '/' at the front of "packorder".
I suggested this on rgrn for the first time in March 1998.

Adjusting inventory letters helps only within objects of the same kind.

It's a bit of a futile exercise anyway, because in 90% of these accidents
the damage is done by losing the existing contents of the bag, and the
loss of one or two additional objects is neither here nor there.
